The fix handles the null VM service case. Both `'o'` and `'O'` route to the same `debugTogglePlatform()` handler (resident_runner.dart:1726-1728), so they behave identically by construction.

The change I made in `debugTogglePlatform()`:

```dart
if (!supportsServiceProtocol || !isRunningDebug) {
  return false;
}
if (flutterDevices.first!.vmService == null) {
  logger.printStatus('Platform toggle is not supported for this device.');
  return false;
}
```

Previously, when `supportsServiceProtocol` and `isRunningDebug` were both true but `vmService` was null, the very next line (`flutterDevices.first!.vmService!.getFlutterViews()`) would throw a null-check error and crash. Now it detects the null VM service, logs `'Platform toggle is not supported for this device.'` via the status logger, and returns gracefully without throwing.
